  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are derived from a single county in southern Germany and may not generalize to regions with different historical settlement dynamics.",
      "what": "The authors evaluated generalized linear models, generalized additive models, and semi-structured deep distributional regression to model historical settlement patterns in Donau-Ries county, Germany, across four reference years. Using spatial block cross-validation, the study measured how proximity to rivers, forests, and agricultural land relates to residential presence. While classical models produced stable and interpretable distance metrics, incorporating local image context via the semi-structured deep regression framework yielded superior predictive performance.",
      "why": "It demonstrates how to combine interpretable spatial distance covariates with deep learning components, establishing the performance and interpretability trade-offs of hybrid statistical models on historical map series."
    }
